## BOSS PumpKing

At the Kingdom of Horror's 4-1 PumpKing is the BOSS, met on his castle's balcony; beating
him recruits him (`NODES.gdd` §4.5). The boss is this kit — the same class, inherited
(`BossPumpKing : PumpKing`) — fighting on the other side: his head bowls at the player. He is
**not** this protagonist: his HP, damage, poise, magazine and cooldowns are his own row in
`BossTable`, all first-pass. Everything about the fight — the row, the rules his brain
follows, his arena — is in `FOES.gdd` §8.

Since v0.11.0 the Kingdom of Horror is in the world pool, so a run can reach his castle; and
until the other realms have bosses of their own, **he stands in at every realm's 4-1**, on
that realm's boss arena (`FOES.gdd` §8.1). His HP there is his row's × the day: 600 on days
1–10, 720, 900, 1200, and 1800 from day 36.

**The Black Prison on the boss — built v0.12.19 (`Realms.gdd` §13, `FOES.gdd` §8.3):** a boss's
ring fills +10 a second and +5 a point of damage he deals or takes; full, he opens it 5 m ahead
of the player's movement (on a player standing still, on them; out of reach, he closes in
first) and recasts the moment it forms. The boss check's `ProbeBossUlt` proves each rule.
*Until v0.12.19:* His kit has the ultimate (it is side-
agnostic: on his side it holds the player, silences them — skills and items — slows them and
darkens their view; 8 m in radius),
but **his brain never presses Q**. A rule for it is the next step: open it when the player is
within 8 m and his ring is full; recast when the player is near its centre. His ring fills only
from damage he takes, as any boss's. The boss check already proves the kit works for him
(`ProbePrisonTakesSides`).

