## Decisions log

- **(v0.10.11) Bounce or roll, decided by how hard it lands.** The 1.5 m/s threshold, the
  3 m/s² friction and the 6 m/s cap were all already in this document; the code applied the
  bounce every resting tick and so never reached the roll. Fixed toward the document rather
  than the document toward the code: "his head can crash along the slope" needs a roll.
- **(v0.10.11) The roll cap is on speed across, and holds on a slope.** Capping before
  gravity's pull was added let a head run a slope at 6.5 m/s; the cap is now applied to what
  the roll keeps.
- **(v0.10.11) A rolling head does not bounce at a change of slope.** At the foot of a slope
  it used to bounce four times and reach level ground with half its speed.
- **(v0.10.11) Whether a boss's head should roll faster, last longer or be thrown harder is
  boss design** (`FOES.gdd` §8.2) and is not decided; today both heads are the same head.
- **(The Black Prison) The owner's spec, verbatim in spirit:** a circle the size of his head's
  biggest blast; 1 s warning with a visual; 4 s of 50 % speed, 50 % jump height and silence on
  every enemy inside; one random-sized pumpkin flung out about every 0.5 s; a recast that opens
  his big mouth at the centre, blinks him in and sets his head off at its biggest; those inside
  lose all vision but one cell. Decided here, for the owner to overrule:
  - **Cast range 8 m** ("not far from him"): about a level head throw.
  - **Radius 3 m**, the head's real blast (pumping does not grow it). It may feel small.
  - **"Inside" is the blast's own test** (the hit circle touches it), checked every tick: **the
    border is not a wall.** A prison that keeps those caught at the start would be a different
    rule (and a one-line change).
  - **Silence takes skills, not the basic attack** — the usual meaning, and what keeps a player
    caught in a BOSS's prison able to fight back. The seagull's poop counts as its basic
    attack. A skill under way runs its course. Items are not skills.
  - **"One cell around you" is the 3 × 3 cells centred on you: 3 m.** A blinded foe drops the
    player at once and is not told where a blow came from.
  - **The recast's blast: 3 m, twice the head's damage (100), no shove**; it costs no head. The
    shove was dropped because it would throw the prisoners out of the prison.
  - **The blast does not end the prison**; a late recast is waited for.
  - **One prison at a time; the recast is once.** Q in the warning does nothing.
  - **Pumpkins: eight, 10–25 damage, no shove, flung outward from the centre**; they can hit
    what stands outside.
  - **Soul Form obeys move-speed shares** (a fix the prison needed: a soul flew through it).

- **(v0.12.13) The owner's answers on the Black Prison:**
  - **"4 s: a slowed enemy just walks out"** — the size is that rule. Decided here, for the
    owner to overrule (TBD #86): it is measured against the standard fighter (10 m/s) — the
    owner spoke of later multiplayer, where the prisoner is a fighter — and "walks out" is the
    game's own test (the hit circle clear of the rim), hence 19.1 m and not 20. *(Superseded in
    v0.12.15: the owner found it too big and set 8 m.)*
  - **His head's blast stays his head's:** the recast's blast, the mouth and the pumpkins keep
    the old 3 m — a 100-damage blast over 19 m would be another ultimate.
  - **"A prisoner can't see its border — their whole map is another world"** — the owner allows
    it to wait for multiplayer. Now: the border is hidden from a prisoner, the veil stands for
    the other world past one cell (TBD #87).
  - **"Silenced, items can't be used"** — a held item's skill is refused, nothing spent; its
    passive goes on.
  - **"Each character's ult energy is their own and is not cleared when a level ends"** — kept
    on the run record, through switches, days and saves; a new run and a new recruit start empty.
- **(2026-11-28) The realm design** (`Realms.gdd`): the prison becomes a sub-realm; only
  silence inside; the caster is pulled in too; nothing crosses its border; random pumpkins;
  BOSS PumpKing will cast it with a boss's ring. Not built yet.
- **(v0.12.15) "黑狱太大了，半径改成8m"** — the owner's number replaces the rule; TBD #86 (which run
  to measure by) is moot. A 10 m/s fighter now walks out from the centre in 1.8 s; slow foes
  are still held the whole time.
- **(v0.12.21) The prison is a sub-realm** (`Realms.gdd` §12, built). Replaced: the move and jump
  ×0.5, the 3 m sight, the dark veil, the border hidden by drawing, pumpkins grown at the heart
  and thrown outward (they could hit outside). Decided here, for the owner to overrule:
  - **Invincibility does not keep a body out:** being in another world is where it is, not a
    status (v1.5 skipped the invincible).
  - **The blast is at the mouth, the patch's anchor**, a body's height over its floor, so a crab
    under it takes it from above and its shell doubles it.
  - **Pumpkins grow anywhere within 85 % of the exit border**, so they land among the
    prisoners rather than in the art past the border.
  - **Found:** with the cast range and the radius both 8 m he is always in his own circle when he
    casts it; he is pulled in unless he steps out in the warning. Flagged to the owner.

